<para>(Students were provided access to Desmos with a set \(x\)-axis of \(-10 &lt; x &lt; 50\) and a set \(y\)-axis of \(-60 &lt; y &lt; 350)\).</para>
<para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(y = -0.93x^2+ 22.63x + 10.48\)</item>
  <item> \(y = -0.69x^2+ 24.83x + 8.07\) </item>
  <item> \(y = -3.11x^2+ 16.32x + 8.94\) </item>
  <item> \(y = -0.7x^2 + 35.93x + 8.19\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y = -0.69x^2+ 24.83x + 8.07\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit.
